  "subtitle": "Crimson skylit room",
  "blurb": "Deep crimson walls under a pitched glass lantern, gilded archways, polished light wood underfoot.",
  "corridorNote": "The reference photograph for this corridor is Room 32 at the National Gallery, London — the Julia and Hans Rausing Room — not a British Museum gallery; the corridor follows it faithfully. Deep crimson walls behind large gold-framed works, a pitched arched glass skylight running the length of the room on white ribs, vaulted ceiling sections in warm red and gold divided by intricate gilded archways, polished light wood floor, dark tufted leather seating down the centre. The collection hung here is the British Museum's own painted holdings, which are prints, frescoes, scrolls and painted papyri rather than gallery canvases.",
